 "In this way, banks permeate the capillaries of the economy, gathering scattered small sums into a great pool and channeling them to where money is urgently needed.",
 "Precisely because banks are so closely tied to the money bags of countless households, every move they make attracts special attention from regulators, and whether capital is sufficient and risk control is strict are repeatedly examined under the spotlight.",
